Relationship to the original
----------------------------

QBlocker4arm is not a copy of the original source code. It was written against
modern toolchains because the 2016 codebase — Swift 2, CocoaPods, Intel-only —
can no longer be compiled with a current version of Xcode. This port:

  * targets Apple Silicon (arm64) and macOS 13 or later;
  * uses Swift 5 and carries no third-party dependencies;
  * replaces LSSharedFileList login items with SMAppService;
  * replaces Realm with a small Codable store, and drops DevMateKit's
    analytics and auto-update entirely;
  * replaces the custom tab bar with NSTabViewController;
  * adds an Input Monitoring permission step and recovers the keyboard event
    tap when macOS throttles it.

Where the original's class and file organisation were carried across, that is an
acknowledgement of its structure, not a claim of independent authorship.


